# The index-side twin of t60. `aot_index_get` mirrored the VM's four
# (target, index) branches but omitted its final else, so ANY unindexable
# target answered null instead of raising "cannot index <type>" — null
# above all. Found while fixing the #898 dot read (ouroboros#96); the two
# need separate files because the first raise ends the program.

xs is [10, 20, 30]
print of xs[1]
d is {"k": "v"}
print of d["k"]
print of d["missing"]

n is null
print of n["k"]
print of "UNREACHABLE — the VM stops above; an AOT that prints this is the bug"
